  "id": "voice-disorder",
  "term": "voice disorder",
  "definition": "A voice disorder is a problem with the voice that is not captured fully by objective measures alone, because it also involves how much difficulty or disability the person experiences. In practice, it is understood partly by how well someone can speak with their voice in everyday work and social situations.",
